4.1 Interface (facade)

// provider.ts
import { BillingPeriodT, PlanTierT, PaymentMethodSummaryT, UpgradeResponseT } from "./types";

export interface BillingProvider {
  // Sessions
  createUpgradeSession(args: {
    workspaceId: string;
    workspaceSlug: string;
    currentPlan: PlanTierT | string;
    plan: PlanTierT;
    period: BillingPeriodT;
    baseUrl: string;
    onboarding?: string;
    userId: string;
    userEmail: string;
  }): Promise<UpgradeResponseT>;

  createPortalSession(args: {
    workspaceId: string;
    workspaceSlug: string;
    returnUrl: string;
    mode: "manage" | "cancel" | "updatePaymentMethod";
  }): Promise<{ redirectUrl: string }>;

  // Payment methods
  listPaymentMethods(args: { workspaceId: string }): Promise<PaymentMethodSummaryT[]>;
  addPaymentMethod(args: {
    workspaceId: string;
    method?: "sepa_debit" | "us_bank_account" | "acss_debit" | "card" | "link";
    returnUrl: string;
  }): Promise<{ redirectUrl: string }>;

  // Subscription invoices (provider side)
  listSubscriptionInvoices(args: { workspaceId: string }):
    Promise<{
      id: string;
      total: number;
      createdAt: Date;
      description: string;
      pdfUrl?: string;
      status?: "paid" | "failed" | "pending";
    }[]>;
}

Reasoning:
The LF UI/API depend only on BillingProvider. Stripe details (prices, portal flows) remain in the stripe adapter. This aligns with the need to remove provider coupling seen in current endpoints (e.g., direct stripe.* calls).

4.2 Stripe Adapter (current provider)

Location: apps/web/lib/billing-lf/providers/stripe.ts
	•	Implements BillingProvider using the existing stripe client.
	•	Preserves security checks like domain allow‑list for return URLs (today's APP_DOMAIN check in the upgrade route).
	•	Encodes "active subscription → portal flow" vs "new/paused → checkout session" decision (same behavior currently implemented in /upgrade).
	•	Returns normalized response objects.

Potential side effects:
	•	We will not pass raw Stripe objects to clients anymore. This breaks any LF consumer that expects Stripe.PaymentMethod objects (the current usePaymentMethods does) — so the LF hooks must switch to normalized types (see §6).

4.3 Invoice merge strategy

Location: apps/web/lib/billing-lf/invoices.ts
	•	Orchestrates provider.listSubscriptionInvoices() and prisma.invoice.findMany(...) for partner payouts & domain renewals, consistent with existing behavior.
	•	Maps results to InvoiceItemT.

Critical decision: keep the hybrid model: provider is source of truth for subscriptions; our DB is SoT for partner payouts / domain renewals.

4.4 Usage service (Tinybird)

Location: apps/web/lib/billing-lf/usage.ts
	•	Wrap the Tinybird query used today (v2_usage pipe via tb.buildPipe) behind a simple getUsage({workspaceId, resource, start,end,timezone}) returning UsagePointT[].
	•	Preserve current cycle date calculation approach used by useUsage() (first/last day based on billingCycleStart).

